# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# Syntax: a URL pattern, then indented "Name: value" lines. Limits are 100
# rules and 2,000 characters per line, so this is nowhere near them.
#
# X-Robots-Tag does what a <meta name="robots"> tag cannot: it applies to the
# PHOTOS too. A meta tag only exists inside HTML, so image files would still be
# indexable without this.
#
#   noindex       do not list this in search results
#   nofollow      do not follow links out of it
#   noarchive     do not keep a cached copy
#   nosnippet     do not show an extract in results
#   noimageindex  do not index the images
#
# Referrer-Policy must NOT be "no-referrer". OpenStreetMap's tile servers
# require a Referer header identifying the site, and serve an "Access blocked"
# image - as HTTP 200, so nothing looks wrong in the console - in place of every
# map tile without one. See https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Blocked_tiles
# "strict-origin" sends only https://yl-trips-site.pages.dev, never the trip
# path or a photo filename. A page opened from disk over file:// sends no
# Referer whatever this says, so its OpenStreetMap basemap stays blocked.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
